    description: "FOUND 2026-09-18 while pinning the WI-romuh pairing fixture (recorded rust-analyzer 1.94.0 output for aardvark-dns @4444d90fee, committed under packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/recorded/). Under the ADR-0057 §10 anchors, 148 of 169 SCIP definitions pair one-to-one with a live rust.py record; of the 21 that do not, 18 are module namespaces (no tree-sitter counterpart by design) and THREE are declarations rust.py emits NO Symbol for at all:\n\n  src/error.rs:3        pub type AardvarkResult<T> = Result<T, AardvarkError>;   (type alias)\n  src/server/serve.rs:38    type ThreadHandleMap<Ip> = ...                        (type alias)\n  src/server/serve.rs:291   static DNSBACKEND: OnceLock<ArcSwap<DNSBackend>> = ...  (static item)\n\nrust.py emits struct / enum / trait / field / function / method / variable (module-level `const` and `let`? — verify which) but no record for `type_item` or `static_item`. Every consumer that asks \"which symbol is declared at this line\" — slice anchoring, the ADR-0057 merge pass, dead-code — gets nothing for a type alias or a static, while the SCIP arm sees both. Same shape as WI-tahot (Go package-level const gets no Symbol).\n\nFIX SHAPE: in rust.py's item walk, emit a Symbol for `type_item` (kind: the registered alias/type kind — check ADR-0027's symbol-kind registry for the value the other analyzers use for aliases; cpp's `using S = ...` is the precedent, INV-sibij) and for `static_item` (kind=variable, like module-level const/let if those are emitted). Then AARDVARK_DNS_PAIRING in the recorded module moves 148 -> 151 and unpaired_class/unpaired_variable -> 0; update the pin with the measurement, do not hand-edit it.\n\nACCEPTANCE: test_recorded_fixtures.py::test_pairing_under_the_declared_rule pins 151/169 with the three names gone from the leftovers; a unit test in test_rust_analyzer.py (mainstream) covers a `type` alias and a `static` on a minimal source."  # 6276
